#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231379 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231453 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c20e9719-4699-5c80-92a1-714717021bb1" :knowledge-point/title "Reading Argmax and Argmin From a Table"}] :question/id #uuid "de77d46f-0d04-510d-951e-650c9ae456fa" :question/math-academy-id "e-22129" :question/problem "| $x$ | $f(x)$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-2$ | $3$ |\n| $-1$ | $0$ |\n| $0$ | $5$ |\n| $1$ | $-1$ |\n| $2$ | $2$ |\n\nThe table above gives values of $f$ on the set $S=\\{-2,-1,0,1,2\\}.$ Use the table to compute\n\n$$\n\\max_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\min_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\arg\\min_{x \\in S} f(x).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- $\\max\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is the maximum output value, while\n\n- $\\arg\\max\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that maximum output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- $\\min\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is the minimum output value, while\n\n- $\\arg\\min\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that minimum output occurs.\n\nThe output values in the table are $3,0,5,-1,$ and $2.$\n\nThe largest output is $5,$ and it occurs at $x=0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)=5\n\\qquad \\textrm{and} \\qquad\n\\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)=0.\n$$\n\nThe smallest output is $-1,$ and it occurs at $x=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\min_{x \\in S} f(x)=-1\n\\qquad \\textrm{and} \\qquad\n\\arg\\min_{x \\in S} f(x)=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231380 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231454 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "23320907-6b2d-5956-82ab-fdd5c5014613" :knowledge-point/title "Reading Argmax and Argmin From a Graph"}] :question/id #uuid "5fe9ded3-34fb-5bf2-a2f4-9598e6cf2d57" :question/math-academy-id "e-22130" :question/problem "![](images/eb/eb6079ac70816cd56061b8b353cc734176eed1698c50376a2e7a34c40f582a89.png)\n\nLet $S=\\{0,1,2,3,4\\}.$ The graph above shows the value of $f(x)$ for each $x \\in S.$ Use the graph to compute\n\n$$\n\\max_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\min_{x \\in S} f(x),\\qquad \\arg\\min_{x \\in S} f(x).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- $\\max\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is the maximum output value, while\n\n- $\\arg\\max\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that maximum output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- $\\min\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is the minimum output value, while\n\n- $\\arg\\min\\limits_{x \\in S} f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that minimum output occurs.\n\nFrom the graph, the highest point has $y$-coordinate $5,$ and it occurs at $x=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)=\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{5}\n\\qquad \\textrm{and} \\qquad\n\\arg\\max_{x \\in S} f(x)=\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{1}.\n$$\n\nThe lowest point has $y$-coordinate $0,$ and it occurs at $x=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\min_{x \\in S} f(x)=\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{0}\n\\qquad \\textrm{and} \\qquad\n\\arg\\min_{x \\in S} f(x)=\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231739 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231454 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "23320907-6b2d-5956-82ab-fdd5c5014613" :knowledge-point/title "Reading Argmax and Argmin From a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ab05338-fc54-52ba-b057-c2351016ab93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ab05338-fc54-52ba-b057-c2351016ab93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533473} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8a34b87-d28c-5563-87ad-3603df605273" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186231024} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "