estion/problem "![](images/68/68b36fbb370ee2d0fe18ad08d0864ef9d127abded1fc6d1c113009cd865feb1b.png)\n\nLet $T=\\{-1,0,1,2,3\\}.$ The graph above shows the value of $h(x)$ for each $x\\in T.$ Assuming that all the dots have integer coordinates, compute the following:\n\n${max}_{x\\in T}h(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in T}h(x)=$\n{{field-2}}\n\n${min}_{x\\in T}h(x)=$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in T}h(x)=$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the maximum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that maximum output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the minimum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that minimum output occurs.\n\nFrom the graph, \n\n- the highest point is at $(2,5),$ so ${max}_{x\\in T}h(x)=5$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in T}h(x)=2,$ and\n\n- the lowest point is at $(0,1),$ so ${min}_{x\\in T}h(x)=1$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in T}h(x)=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231740 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231453 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c20e9719-4699-5c80-92a1-714717021bb1" :knowledge-point/title "Reading Argmax and Argmin From a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8dcb2bc7-0c83-5cd7-b92d-1467a3f52d63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8dcb2bc7-0c83-5cd7-b92d-1467a3f52d63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533481} :answer-field/id #uuid "939237bf-2795-5991-9195-c9aac7c4a8ec" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186231028} {:answer-field/choices [{:an