id "q-355222" :question/problem "| $t$ | $h(t)$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-3$ | $2$ |\n| $-1$ | $-1$ |\n| $0$ | $-5$ |\n| $2$ | $4$ |\n| $5$ | $0$ |\n\nThe table above gives values of a function $h$ on the set $T=\\{-3,-1,0,2,5\\}.$ Compute the following:\n\n${max}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-2}}\n\n${min}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the maximum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that maximum output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the minimum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that minimum output occurs.\n\nThe output values are $2,-1,-5,4,$ and $0.$ The maximum output is $4$ (at $t=2$), and the minimum output is $-5$ (at $t=0$). \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{max}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =4 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =2 \\\\ {min}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =-5 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533996 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231453 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c20e9719-4699-5c80-92a1-714717021bb1" :knowledge-point/title "Reading Argmax and Argmin From a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "024efc4a-64e6-5e5a-91b3-6066df824ce9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "024efc4a-64e6-5e5a-91b3-6066df824ce9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533135} :answer-field/id #uuid "169b2abe-c737-5c1b-9e4b-b658560396dc" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218604549