difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3ad87e41-53b3-5b37-8281-b66e69b1893c" :question/math-academy-id "q-355223" :question/problem "| $t$ | $g(t)$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-4$ | $-2$ |\n| $-2$ | $1$ |\n| $2$ | $-1$ |\n| $3$ | $5$ |\n\nThe table above gives values of a function $g$ on the set $T=\\{-4,-2,2,3\\}.$ Compute the following:\n\n${max}_{t\\in T}g(t)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{t\\in T}g(t)=$\n{{field-2}}\n\n${min}_{t\\in T}g(t)=$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{t\\in T}g(t)=$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the maximum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that maximum output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the minimum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that minimum output occurs.\n\nThe output values are $-2,1,-1,$ and $5.$ The maximum output is $5$ (at $t=3$), and the minimum output is $-2$ (at $t=-4$). \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{max}_{t\\in T}g(t) & =5 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{t\\in T}g(t) & =3 \\\\ {min}_{t\\in T}g(t) & =-2 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{t\\in T}g(t) & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534010 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231453 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c20e9719-4699-5c80-92a1-714717021bb1" :knowledge-point/title "Reading Argmax and Argmin From a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65d28be8-31bb-5262-a843-334f239a7d69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533377}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65d28be8-31bb-5262-a843-334f239a7d69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533377} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ce9c35d-ca22-5837-8b4f-f769d3560c4b